  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\r\n\r\nSearch for the term \"DNS name\" on https://spec.matrix.org/v1.11/server-server-api.\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nThe SS API uses the term \"DNS name\" in a number of places, for instance when describing the `{serverName}` path component in [`GET /_matrix/key/v2/query/{serverName}`](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.11/server-server-api/#get_matrixkeyv2queryservername).\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-07-18 at 09 45 46](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/37292a27-21fe-4978-acae-bc553101ac2f)\r\n\r\nThe appendices in turn define a \"DNS name\" as one possible option for the `hostname` part of [\"server names\"](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.11/appendices/#server-name).\r\n\r\nI suspect that the SS API merely uses the term \"DNS name\" as a transliteration of the \"server name\" term defined in the appendices. To avoid any confusion though, I think it might be better to just stick to \"server name\" and link out to its definition in the appendices.\r\n",
